From: WG2600HP / IPQ8064 / OpenWrt 25.12.6
Subject: [PATCH] nss-gmac: allow QCA8337 DSA CPU tag overhead on WG2600HP only

Linux 6.12 ether_setup() initializes max_mtu=ETH_DATA_LEN (1500), and
alloc_etherdev() inherits this limit. The QCA8337 DSA conduit increases
the master MTU by the length of the internal tag. The previous RAM image
reported eth0/eth1 -EINVAL while raising conduit MTU to 1502 with the
legacy QCA tag. The integrated qca-8021q tagger requires VLAN_HLEN=4.

Set the maximum permissible conduit MTU to 1504 on the WG2600HP only.
Keep the configured MTU and all other boards unchanged. The existing
nss_gmac_change_mtu() / NSS physical data-plane operation remains
responsible for actually accepting the requested MTU; firmware
acceptance and throughput remain hardware-test requirements.

The matching context was checked against a public nss-gmac reference;
exact pinned 17176794 source patch application and ARM compile still
require independent verification. Not a firmware build or G2 PASS.

--- a/ipq806x/nss_gmac_ctrl.c
+++ b/ipq806x/nss_gmac_ctrl.c
@@ -37,4 +37,5 @@
 #include <linux/workqueue.h>
 #include <linux/phy.h>
 #include <linux/net_tstamp.h>
+#include <linux/if_vlan.h>
 #include <asm/div64.h>
@@ -1175,7 +1176,16 @@
 	netdev = alloc_etherdev(sizeof(struct nss_gmac_dev));
 	if (!netdev) {
 		pr_info("%s: alloc_etherdev() failed\n", __func__);
 		return -ENOMEM;
 	}
 
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_OF
+	/* DSA qca-8021q adds a four-byte tag on both CPU conduits.
+	 * Permit only the tag overhead, not a user-facing jumbo MTU.
+	 */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("nec,wg2600hp"))
+		netdev->max_mtu = ETH_DATA_LEN + VLAN_HLEN;
+#endif
+
 	gmacdev = netdev_priv(netdev);
